# Cra draws Arc's Picture in Picture controls over Chromium's PiP window and keeps Chromium's own
# (title, ±10 s, scrubber) away by never letting that window take the pointer or become key: a key
# PiP window shows Chrome's controls on every mouse move, so two sets showed at once (GitHub #262).
# Cra set Chromium's `preventKeyWindow` once, but Chromium writes it too: a window it orders in on
# another Space gets NO back when the Space changes. Here it is cleared that way and the window
# asked to become key; the switch must be back on and the window not key. (A background test copy
# can't make any window key, so Cra handing the key back when it gets it anyway is a release check.)
# promise: #262
cra://open?url=file://${FIXTURES}/Pages/video.html
expect-log loaded file:
wait 2
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"document.getElementById('v').requestPictureInPicture().then(()=>'pip:open')","awaitPromise":true,"userGesture":true}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*"value":"pip:open"
wait 1
cra://debug?pip=open
expect-log Cra pip open: windows=1 key=0 appKey=0 mouse=0 preventKey=1
cra://debug?pipKey=space
wait 1
cra://debug?pip=space
expect-log Cra pip space: windows=1 key=0 appKey=0 mouse=0 preventKey=1
